# 7 Sep 2026, fifth bump. Diffed as a parsed schema tree, not as text — the
# defects that made that necessary are on yuvoy-api#92 and #103. PURELY
# ADDITIVE: three new paths, one new schema, nothing removed, no `required:`
# list grown, no requestBody made required.
#
# Consumed in this change:
#   - `POST /media/photo-intents` + `.../complete` — a listing can hold
#     photographs (yuvoy-operator#27). From `complete` onward a photograph
#     travels the SAME road as a clip: the same rights attestation, the same
#     moderation queue, the same publish gate. Deliberately not a second
#     pipeline, so there is no weaker way round the first.
#   - `GET /catalog/vocabulary` — the fix for yuvoy-api#113. The create form's
#     category and destination were two text boxes seeded from the operator's
#     own listings, which was a dead end for their FIRST listing. Both are now
#     pickers with the labels a person uses.
#
# Learned from the publish 409's description rather than asked: photographs and
# clips have SEPARATE ceilings of 20 each, and `details.kind` / `details.limit`
# say which one was reached. The attach form now names the right one.
#
# Known gap, raised rather than worked around: `GET /media` returns no `kind`,
# so the operator's own library cannot tell a photograph from a clip. Inferring
# it from an absent `durationSeconds` would mislabel a clip that is still
# processing, so nothing here claims a kind at all.
